  "caption_candidate": "Figure 1. From photographs to ecological comparisons. (a–c) Public Cirsium photographs with stored capitulum detector boxes. These archived source examples illustrate the measurement pipeline; their membership in the current V4 analytical cohorts is not asserted. (d–f) The boxed C. pannonicum head in (a) illustrates image-referenced orientation, floral colour and projected outline measurement. The arrow in (d) marks image top, not gravity; the displayed 0.7° is the archived production value 0.732009° rounded to one decimal place. In (e), the white boundary outlines the archived floral-pixel mask. In (f), red marks the contour, yellow its convex hull and blue the principal axis. Values are frozen head-level outputs. The eight constructs comprise angle, lightness, chroma, circular hue, aspect ratio, circularity, solidity and width-profile coefficient of variation (CV); hue uses two numerical coordinates. No example CV value is supplied by the archived panel table, so its definition is given in Table S2.1. Eligible head measurements are summarised within photographic records by domain; the sets of contributing heads can differ among domains. These linked records support the three ecological comparisons. Panels are cropped and annotated derivatives of the archived photographs; no new image measurements were used. Photo (a) and derivatives (d–f): © Bobo-X, CC BY 4.0, https://www.inaturalist.org/photos/532420148, https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/. Photo (b): uploaded by Jesse Rorabaugh, CC0 1.0, https://www.inaturalist.org/photos/4051162. Photo (c): uploaded by Diego Blanco, CC0 1.0, https://www.inaturalist.org/photos/475732253. CC0 declaration: https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/.",
  "verification_notes": [
    "Original source photo pages and public API photo objects were read without credentials on 2026-10-30. Only image-specific attribution/license evidence was retained; no coordinates or protected source records are included.",
